## Key Improvements
### All Platforms (Including Git Bash)
- ✅ Beautiful Unicode symbols render correctly
- ✅ Clean, professional appearance
- ✅ Proper alignment and spacing
- ✅ Cursor hidden during interaction
- ✅ Consistent across all terminals
### What Changed
1. **Unicode Support**: Git Bash actually supports Unicode perfectly - we now use it everywhere
2. **Cursor Hiding**: Cursor is hidden during prompt interaction for cleaner UI
3. **Consistent Rendering**: Same beautiful symbols on all platforms
## Symbol Reference
t:10(Element,Symbol,Description)[Active Step,`◆`,Current active prompt Completed Step,`◇`,Submitted/completed prompt Vertical Bar,`│`,Left border Top Corner,`┌`,Start of prompt sequence Bottom Corner,`└`,End of prompt section Radio Selected,`●`,Selected radio option Radio Unselected,`○`,Unselected radio option Checkbox Checked,`◼`,Selected checkbox Checkbox Unchecked,`◻`,Unselected checkbox Password Mask,`•`,Password character mask]
## Testing in Your Environment
To see the symbols in your terminal, run:
```bash
cargo run --example test_symbols --manifest-path crates/cli/Cargo.toml
```
Expected output:
```
=== Terminal Environment Detection ===
MSYSTEM: Ok("MINGW64")
...
=== Symbol Set ===
Using Unicode symbols on all platforms
=== Symbol Preview ===
Step Active: ◆
Step Submit: ◇
Bar Start: ┌
Bar: │
Bar End: └
Radio Active: ●
Radio Inactive: ○
Checkbox Active: ◻
Checkbox Selected: ◼
Password Mask: •
```
## Additional Features
### Cursor Management
- Cursor automatically hidden when prompts are active
- Restored when prompts complete (submit/cancel/error)
- Applies to all prompt types and animations
- Creates a cleaner, more professional interface
### Platform Compatibility
- ✅ Git Bash (MINGW64) on Windows
- ✅ Windows Terminal
- ✅ ConEmu
- ✅ CMD (with Unicode support)
- ✅ PowerShell
- ✅ Unix/Linux/macOS terminals
- ✅ All modern terminal emulators